        <item>
            <title>1.2.0</title>
            <pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 09:53:17 -0400</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>1.2.0</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.2.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[### Paste several screenshots at once

In the panel, hold **⇧** and use the arrow keys to pick a run of screenshots,
GIFs or recordings, then press **Return** and they all paste, one after
another, in the order you see them. **⌘-click** adds or removes one, **⇧-click**
stretches the run to the one you click, and **esc** lets go of the set. The
same rules as Finder, up to ten at a time.

Into a terminal they arrive as one line of file paths, which is what a command
line, or a coding assistant running in one, can use.

### Recording, smoothed out

- **A 3-2-1 countdown** after you press Record, so the video starts with you
  ready rather than with your hand on its way to the thing you are showing.
  Tap the shortcut again during it to call it off.
- **Stop appears where Record was.** It is under your pointer when the
  recording begins, instead of somewhere different every time, and never
  hidden behind the Dock on a full-screen recording.
- **Your first click counts.** The app you are recording now has focus the
  moment recording starts, so a click lands on what you clicked, not on
  waking the window up.
- **Showing clicks is your choice.** A new button beside the microphone on the
  Record screen turns the click rings on or off. Cubby remembers which you
  prefer.

### Sharper GIFs

GIFs are now made at the size the recording looked on your screen, where
before they came out at a little over half of it. Small text in a GIF is
readable again. The files are larger for it, roughly twice the size; trimming
a clip first is still the best way to keep one small.
]]></description>
